---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getJobs, formatSpan, currentTitle, getCurrentNote } from '~/lib/content';
import { externalLinkProps } from '~/lib/links';
import portrait from '~/assets/images/me.jpg';
import cosplay from '~/assets/images/me2.jpg';

/**
 * The career timeline here is generated from the same `jobs` collection the
 * resume page reads. The prose around it is Phase 3's.
 */
const jobs = await getJobs('site');
const currentNote = await getCurrentNote();

const w4GamesAnnouncement =
  'https://www.w4games.com/blog/w4-games-news-1/second-dinner-studios-becomes-a-strategic-investor-in-w4-games-and-plans-to-build-the-largest-game-in-godot-yet-37';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="How Ali Wallick got into games, and the four studios since: Kaneva, Red 5 Studios, MobilityWare, and Second Dinner."
  image="/og/home.jpg"
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  {
    /* The one page on the site where a face is the obvious content. `me.jpg`
      is a real headshot as of #64/#70 — replaced the full-body hiking shot
      that used to stand in this slot, whose face was a few dozen pixels
      inside a 12rem circle. `.portrait img` crops to square with
      `object-fit: cover` so whatever gets dropped in here next doesn't have
      to be pre-cropped.

      Real alt text, unlike the project thumbnails: this is not duplicating
      adjacent link text, so the model's guard applies normally. */
  }
  <figure class="portrait">
    <Image src={portrait} alt="Ali Wallick" widths={[180, 360]} sizes="12rem" loading="eager" />
  </figure>

  <p>
    Born and raised in Miami, I got interested in games young. Young enough that at seven I burned
    through my family's long-distance minutes calling my uncle for advice on <em>Myst</em>. In high
    school I found the Computational Media program at Georgia Tech: computer science and digital
    media, in equal parts. I discovered my love for programming there, especially front-end work,
    where I get to combine the logic of programming with the creativity of design. I took every game
    development class I could find and went to Global Game Jam and the Microsoft College Puzzle
    Challenge. I graduated in 2011 with one goal: get into the games industry.
  </p>

  <p>
    That's mostly what the rest of this page is. I've been at it since 2011, nearly all of it in UI
    and systems engineering. Four years at Kaneva, where I went from a new engineer to leading the
    UI team. Then a year on a much bigger PC shooter at Red 5 Studios, and three years shipping
    casino mobile games at MobilityWare. In 2019 I joined Second Dinner as the studio's 11th
    employee. I spent five years on{' '}
    <a href="/projects/marvel-snap">Marvel Snap</a>, which shipped in October 2022. {currentNote}{
      ' '
    }
    Second Dinner has said as much{' '}
    <a href={w4GamesAnnouncement} {...externalLinkProps(w4GamesAnnouncement)}>publicly</a>. Beyond
    that, it's not mine to talk about yet.
  </p>

  <h2>Where I've worked</h2>
  <ul class="project-list">
    {
      jobs.map((job) => (
        <li>
          <strong>{currentTitle(job)}</strong>, {job.data.company}
          <p class="meta">
            {job.data.location} · {formatSpan(job.data.start, job.data.end)}
          </p>
          {job.data.summary && <p>{job.data.summary}</p>}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Off the clock</h2>

  {
    /* `me2.jpg`, also unused since the Phase 3 migration, and the strongest
      image argument on this page — it is the Kerbal Space Program cosplay whose
      Dragon Con win the paragraph below already describes. An image that
      illustrates a sentence already on the page earns its place in a way a
      decorative one never does, which is why this slot is more convincing than
      the portrait above it despite being the smaller file. */
  }
  <figure class="aside-figure">
    <Image
      src={cosplay}
      alt="Kerbal Space Program cosplay — oversized green kerbal heads in white space helmets"
      widths={[300, 600]}
      sizes="14rem"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </figure>

  <p>
    Most of my free time goes to my family, including my young daughter and our pets. The rest goes
    to games, reading, camping, cooking, baking, and crafting, usually with friends along the way.
    I'm a longtime science fiction and fantasy fan, in books and on screen. I still make time for
    game jams and personal projects on the side. Away from the computer I gravitate toward hands-on,
    creative things. Costuming is one of them, including a Best Group Costume win at Dragon Con for
    a <em>Kerbal Space Program</em> cosplay.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
